BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Motivational Interviewing 2-Day workshop
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261208
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261209
DTSTAMP:20261127T195042Z
UID:dartmouth-83177@free-food-dartmouth
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://home.dartmouth.edu/events/eve
 nt?event=83177\nhttps://forms.gle/MUtMqUie1dGKRXzH8\nhttps://dialogues.dar
 tmouth.edu/\nhttp://dartgo.org/swc\nhttps://mentalhealth.dartmouth.edu/str
 ategic-plan/commitment-care\n\nDescription:\nWinterim 2026 Motivational In
 terviewing Training—Register by December 1 here:\nhttps://forms.gle/MUtM
 qUie1dGKRXzH8\nDartmouth Dialogues\n: Motivational Interviewing Two-Day Wo
 rkshop\nTuesday\, December 8 and Friday\, December 11*\n9 a.m.–4:30 p.m.
  (morning refreshments available at 8:30 a.m.)\nLocation: Berry 180A\; the
  LINK classroom. First Floor Berry Library.\nThe\nStudent Wellness Center\
 n\, with support from Dartmouth Dialogues\, offers this intensive\, intera
 ctive (and fun!) two-day workshop aimed at building basic proficiency in M
 otivational Interviewing (MI). MI is a collaborative communication style f
 or supporting individuals through growth and change.\nMI trainings are nam
 ed in Dartmouth's\nCommitment to Care strategic plan\nas “effective skil
 l-building trainings that support high-quality mentoring\, advising\, and 
 teaching.”\nThis evidence-based approach has broad application for worki
 ng with students (and others) and can be an instrumental tool for advisors
 \, coaches\, facilitators\, and educators.\nThe training is free and open 
 to the entire Dartmouth community. Morning refreshments\, snacks\, and lun
 ch will be provided.\nFacilitated by Caitlin Barthelmes\, member of the MI
  Network of Trainers and LB White of the Student Wellness Center.\n*Please
  attend both days. We offer this training twice a year. If you can't commi
 t to the full training this time\, please plan to attend the event when it
  is offered next summer.\n\nSponsor / organizer: Student Wellness Center\n
 \nAudience: Public\n\nSource: Dartmouth\n\nWhy this was included: explicit
  food-service wording\; food keyword near service context\n\nFood availabi
 lity is inferred from the source listing\; verify details before attending
 .
LAST-MODIFIED:20261127T195042Z
LOCATION:Berry Library\, LINK classroom
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://home.dartmouth.edu/events/event?event=83177
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
END:VEVENT
